WEBVTT

00:13.854 --> 00:18.191
<i>I've met plenty of people who turned out</i>
<i>to be nice once I talked to them.</i>

00:18.775 --> 00:21.695
People often said I was hard to approach.

00:24.781 --> 00:27.993
I'm terrible at starting conversations.

00:28.076 --> 00:30.203
I'm glad we can talk about manga together.

00:33.290 --> 00:37.711
It's been boring
because there's no one I click with.

00:41.339 --> 00:42.591
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:43.091 --> 00:45.802
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Thank you. Thank you.

00:46.636 --> 00:47.763
<i>Don't mention it.</i>

00:49.431 --> 00:53.560
<i>If the environment is partly to blame</i>
<i>for the isolation,</i>

00:54.644 --> 00:56.021
<i>I would…</i>

00:57.564 --> 00:58.565
HAMBURGER BOM BOM

00:58.648 --> 00:59.816
Yeah. Then, this guy…

00:59.900 --> 01:02.235
Amamiya? You listening?

01:03.528 --> 01:04.696
'Course I am.

01:05.447 --> 01:06.948
<i>Oh, well.</i>

02:38.540 --> 02:42.961
EPISODE 2
LOCKSMITH

02:43.545 --> 02:45.088
Join us for a good time.

02:45.172 --> 02:46.214
No, thanks!

02:46.840 --> 02:47.841
<i>What do I even do?</i>

02:47.924 --> 02:49.259
TWO AGAINST ONE
WHAT IF I UPSET THEM

02:49.342 --> 02:50.343
<i>I'm terrified and angry.</i>

02:50.427 --> 02:51.720
THEY'RE MOCKING ME
WHAT A WASTE OF TIME

02:52.304 --> 02:53.722
- <i>How frustrating.</i>
- Let's go.

02:53.805 --> 02:55.015
- Come with us.
- It's gonna be fun.

02:55.098 --> 02:57.809
I said I'm not interested!

02:59.060 --> 03:01.813
I'm serious. Leave me alone.

03:04.816 --> 03:05.859
Bye.

03:08.320 --> 03:09.905
Sorry. You okay?

03:11.990 --> 03:13.241
I thought it was you.

03:14.784 --> 03:16.077
Mr. Giraffe?

03:16.828 --> 03:18.246
I HAVE TO TAKE THE CROSSWALK
OVER THERE TO GET TO THIS SIDE

03:18.330 --> 03:19.664
Sorry I ignored you back there.

03:22.542 --> 03:24.252
Please pretend like we're friends.

03:24.336 --> 03:25.837
I'm sorry,

03:25.921 --> 03:28.840
but please stay with me
until we're out of their sight.

03:29.341 --> 03:30.342
Say what?

03:30.842 --> 03:34.679
I was able to meet up with a friend,
so I'm okay now. Bye!

03:34.763 --> 03:35.764
What?

03:36.973 --> 03:39.392
BLURRY

03:40.435 --> 03:42.145
<i>Does she know them?</i>

03:42.229 --> 03:44.397
<i>Maybe not.</i>

03:45.982 --> 03:47.192
SCURRYING AWAY

03:47.275 --> 03:49.069
High schoolers these days are scary.

03:49.152 --> 03:50.153
Ain't that right.

03:52.739 --> 03:54.407
Thank you so much.

03:54.991 --> 03:57.911
Huh? I didn't do anything, did I?

03:57.994 --> 04:00.163
Didn't you know them?

04:01.790 --> 04:03.750
They came up to me out of nowhere.

04:04.834 --> 04:06.253
You're so popular.

04:06.753 --> 04:08.421
- It's not like that.
- What?

04:10.215 --> 04:11.383
I mean,

04:11.883 --> 04:14.761
what you saw wasn't like that.

04:15.804 --> 04:20.183
<i>Their vibe was that nothing else mattered</i>
<i>as long as they were having a good time.</i>

04:21.059 --> 04:23.520
Rather, they were looking down on me,

04:23.603 --> 04:26.940
so it's not a situation
I can be happy about. So…

04:30.318 --> 04:33.029
<i>Hold on, why am I defending myself?</i>

04:33.113 --> 04:35.323
<i>I should just play it off.</i>

04:36.449 --> 04:37.701
<i>He's gonna get weirded out.</i>

04:40.245 --> 04:42.998
Should I have punched them?

04:43.790 --> 04:46.251
No, you don't need to take it that far.

04:46.334 --> 04:47.711
Are you sure?

04:48.420 --> 04:52.424
Actually, I'm sorry. It's like
I used you to get away from them.

04:52.924 --> 04:55.719
Why are you apologizing?
It's totally fine.

04:55.802 --> 04:58.847
I wouldn't get upset
over something like this.

05:01.433 --> 05:03.268
Do you live around here, Himuro?

05:03.768 --> 05:05.895
No. I wanted to go
to the community center.

05:05.979 --> 05:08.106
What? That's where I was going too.

05:08.189 --> 05:10.108
Then, why don't we walk together?

05:20.201 --> 05:23.913
Extracurricular activities will be on hold
during the exam preparation period…

05:23.997 --> 05:26.708
- <i>HR is going on forever!</i>
- …so your daily routine may be disrupted.

05:26.791 --> 05:29.878
<i>Koyun, sorry I'm making you wait!</i>

05:31.379 --> 05:32.881
Say…

05:37.093 --> 05:39.554
I'd like to know your name, please.

05:39.637 --> 05:42.849
Right. I never told you my name.

05:42.932 --> 05:43.975
My bad.

05:45.143 --> 05:47.520
You can just call me Yota.

05:47.604 --> 05:49.689
<i>He only gave me his first name.</i>

05:49.773 --> 05:50.774
I WANTED TO KNOW HIS LAST NAME

05:50.857 --> 05:52.776
It's a pleasure to meet you, Himuro.

05:54.152 --> 05:55.278
Sorry.

05:55.361 --> 05:58.865
My last name's actually Hikawa,
not Himuro.

05:58.948 --> 06:00.825
No way! Sorry.

06:00.909 --> 06:02.786
You should've told me sooner.

06:07.082 --> 06:10.293
How much longer is it to get
to the community center?

06:10.376 --> 06:12.212
I'm terrible with maps.

06:12.295 --> 06:14.380
We'll be there in about five minutes.

06:15.215 --> 06:16.299
<i>Five minutes.</i>

06:17.258 --> 06:19.469
<i>Can we keep</i>
<i>the conversation going for that long?</i>

06:24.766 --> 06:27.811
Hikawa, are you good friends with Miki?

06:28.728 --> 06:31.606
We're childhood friends.

06:31.689 --> 06:34.192
We live close, and we went to the same
elementary and middle school.

06:34.275 --> 06:36.069
Is that so?

06:37.070 --> 06:40.490
We went to the same cram school
in middle school.

06:40.573 --> 06:41.574
What?

06:42.575 --> 06:44.202
<i>They've been friends since middle school?</i>

06:44.285 --> 06:47.455
<i>Does that mean he knows the real Miki?</i>

06:47.539 --> 06:49.124
<i>Now Miki.</i>

06:49.207 --> 06:50.250
You know, Miki,

06:50.834 --> 06:53.711
I liked her much better
the way she used to be.

06:54.295 --> 06:55.547
Me too.

06:55.630 --> 06:56.631
Right?

06:56.714 --> 06:59.175
Honestly, I want to tell everyone
what she's really like.

06:59.259 --> 07:01.386
Seriously, what a waste.

07:02.929 --> 07:04.597
<i>No matter what you're like,</i>

07:04.681 --> 07:07.100
<i>some people will want to stick by you.</i>

07:11.104 --> 07:12.188
You've gotta be kidding.

07:13.273 --> 07:15.275
Hold on, isn't that Yota?

07:16.860 --> 07:17.944
You're right.

07:18.027 --> 07:20.363
But wait. That girl next to him, she's…

07:22.282 --> 07:23.616
What?

07:23.700 --> 07:25.618
MEITEN COMMUNITY CENTER

07:30.206 --> 07:31.749
Here's your seat, Miki.

07:31.833 --> 07:32.917
Thanks.

07:33.001 --> 07:36.254
What the… What kind of pairing is this?

07:37.088 --> 07:38.298
What kind…

07:38.381 --> 07:39.591
Great question.

07:42.510 --> 07:43.511
What?

07:44.179 --> 07:46.139
Hey, I'm the one asking.

07:50.560 --> 07:51.769
Sorry.

07:53.855 --> 07:56.566
Geez! You guys surprised me!

07:56.649 --> 07:59.027
Why didn't you give me a heads up?

07:59.110 --> 08:01.362
I told her not to say anything.

08:01.446 --> 08:02.864
I told her, "Let's surprise Miki!"

08:02.947 --> 08:05.700
You too, Koyun.
Why'd you go along with it?

08:06.618 --> 08:10.580
More importantly,
didn't you punch the jerks who hit on her?

08:11.164 --> 08:13.291
No. Hikawa didn't want me to.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.044
There's no need to go that far.

08:16.127 --> 08:17.170
What?

08:18.296 --> 08:21.382
Are you taking the same train?
I'll walk you to the station.

08:21.466 --> 08:22.842
Thanks!

08:24.302 --> 08:26.596
Yota, do you go to that study room often?

08:26.679 --> 08:28.264
Yeah.

08:28.806 --> 08:31.309
My younger brother and sister
are still little.

08:31.392 --> 08:33.353
It's too noisy at home.

08:33.436 --> 08:35.980
Right. How old are they again?

08:36.064 --> 08:38.525
They're both three years old.
They're twins.

08:39.067 --> 08:40.151
HIS MOM IS SUCH A TROOPER…

08:40.235 --> 08:41.736
<i>That's quite an age gap.</i>

08:42.320 --> 08:44.948
It's partly because
of the toddlers at home,

08:45.031 --> 08:47.242
but I can focus better at the study room.

08:47.325 --> 08:50.620
I feel you. I didn't check my phone today!

08:50.703 --> 08:52.914
I didn't even have space to fool around.

08:52.997 --> 08:54.499
Don't fool around.

08:56.584 --> 08:58.503
Give me a minute.

08:58.586 --> 09:02.257
I need some sugar to recharge
after all the studying I did.

09:03.258 --> 09:05.260
Great idea. I'll grab a drink too.

09:12.225 --> 09:14.310
<i>He's taller than the vending machine.</i>

09:14.394 --> 09:15.520
<i>It must be nice.</i>

09:16.938 --> 09:19.274
<i>I wish I was born that way.</i>

09:19.857 --> 09:21.401
Take your pick, you two.

09:21.484 --> 09:22.652
You don't mind?

09:22.735 --> 09:24.404
I know you want the red bean soup, Miki.

09:24.487 --> 09:26.155
You know me well.

09:26.239 --> 09:28.032
Thanks, Yota.

09:28.116 --> 09:30.159
I'll cover you next time.

09:31.327 --> 09:32.662
Oh, my gosh! Why?

09:33.413 --> 09:37.584
You used a bill, so how'd you
manage to scatter coins everywhere?

09:37.667 --> 09:39.419
My bad.

09:40.336 --> 09:42.338
What do you want to drink, Hikawa?

09:42.422 --> 09:43.673
Me?

09:43.756 --> 09:45.008
I FEEL BAD - SHAKE SHAKE

09:45.091 --> 09:46.301
I…

09:47.719 --> 09:50.221
Here, Miki. You can pick for her.

09:50.305 --> 09:51.514
Leave it to me.

09:52.015 --> 09:55.101
How about a warm corn soup for Koyun?

09:55.184 --> 09:58.563
But I'm craving red bean soup,
so red bean soup it is!

09:58.646 --> 10:00.189
What the heck?

10:00.273 --> 10:04.527
Well, I want her to drink the same thing
so we can both say it's tasty.

10:05.653 --> 10:06.821
You're so selfish.

10:08.114 --> 10:09.574
<i>They really do get along.</i>

10:10.241 --> 10:11.576
RED BEAN SOUP

10:13.328 --> 10:17.999
Like I said earlier,
we went to the same cram school.

10:18.082 --> 10:21.085
Miki, Minato, and I were always together.

10:21.169 --> 10:24.255
Oh, yeah. We used to
eat and talk after cram school.

10:24.756 --> 10:27.759
Mina… You mean Amamiya.

10:27.842 --> 10:30.094
Hold on, Koyun, you know Minato too?

10:30.678 --> 10:33.097
No, not really.

10:33.181 --> 10:34.974
STRETCH

10:35.683 --> 10:38.144
Don't tell me he picked on you again.

10:38.227 --> 10:39.228
Again?

10:41.189 --> 10:43.107
You poor thing.

10:43.191 --> 10:45.318
You can just ignore him.

10:45.401 --> 10:48.613
Yota, do you not get along with Amamiya?

10:49.656 --> 10:51.491
I'm just kidding.

10:53.326 --> 10:55.703
<i>Koyun, Yota and Minato.</i>

10:56.204 --> 10:59.874
Hikawa, do people around you
call you Koyun?

10:59.957 --> 11:00.958
PEOPLE RARELY CALL HER BY NAME

11:01.042 --> 11:02.251
No, only Miki does.

11:02.335 --> 11:04.045
- Koyun.
- Yes?

11:04.128 --> 11:06.005
It's a good nickname.

11:06.089 --> 11:07.382
Right?

11:07.465 --> 11:09.008
Why are you smug about it?

11:09.717 --> 11:12.887
I told you, you can be casual with me.

11:12.970 --> 11:15.056
I don't like people being overly formal.

11:15.139 --> 11:16.933
- No more talking so politely.
- What?

11:17.016 --> 11:18.142
I get it.

11:18.226 --> 11:21.020
I also feel more comfortable
when people are casual.

11:21.104 --> 11:22.980
Is that how it is?

11:24.148 --> 11:25.483
Thank you!

11:26.109 --> 11:28.277
Yota, will you be
at the study room tomorrow too?

11:28.361 --> 11:30.113
Yeah. I'll be there.

11:30.196 --> 11:31.531
Then, see you tomorrow.

11:32.156 --> 11:33.366
See you tomorrow.

11:35.451 --> 11:36.661
'Til tomorrow.

11:52.718 --> 11:55.346
<i>Koyuki Hikawa.</i>

11:58.391 --> 12:00.852
Huh, was there a girl like that?

12:00.935 --> 12:03.688
I think she's Hikawa from Class 2.

12:04.439 --> 12:06.774
Word is, she's always grouchy
and doesn't fit in with her class.

12:13.322 --> 12:16.284
<i>I thought Class 2 was pretty quiet.</i>

12:17.160 --> 12:21.247
<i>Maybe it's more that she can't find</i>
<i>anyone she can relate to.</i>

12:22.665 --> 12:26.752
<i>Since then, I kept following her</i>
<i>with my eyes every time we crossed paths.</i>

12:27.753 --> 12:28.838
<i>She's by herself again.</i>

12:31.966 --> 12:33.092
STRETCH

12:33.843 --> 12:35.386
<i>I always thought,</i>

12:36.554 --> 12:39.390
<i>"What a p…"</i>

12:40.433 --> 12:42.185
INCOMING CALL
NINE AUDIO

12:44.187 --> 12:46.022
<i>Sorry, Minato.</i>

12:46.105 --> 12:47.648
<i>Can we meet right now?</i>

12:47.732 --> 12:49.108
<i>There's something I want to talk about.</i>

12:50.193 --> 12:51.986
Okay. I'll come out.

13:08.794 --> 13:10.254
What's this out of the blue?

13:14.425 --> 13:15.468
You must be cold.

13:20.306 --> 13:21.974
ROYAL MILK TEA

13:22.058 --> 13:23.226
I want to break up.

13:27.939 --> 13:29.232
What makes you say that?

13:32.193 --> 13:33.736
I can't trust you.

13:35.071 --> 13:38.241
You could chalk it up to kindness,

13:39.325 --> 13:44.247
but you never liked me to begin with,
did you, Minato?

13:45.164 --> 13:48.626
I can tell you're not into me.

13:48.709 --> 13:52.463
Did I do something
that made you feel lonely?

13:53.965 --> 13:56.884
Don't respond
to everything with questions.

13:56.968 --> 14:01.013
You always do that.
I want to know how you really feel.

14:07.019 --> 14:08.354
You know what, Minato?

14:09.355 --> 14:12.066
You really don't have a sense of self.

14:15.027 --> 14:16.279
I'm home.

14:17.863 --> 14:21.576
Were you out, Minato?
Was it something urgent?

14:22.285 --> 14:23.286
No.

14:23.953 --> 14:25.538
It was nothing, really.

14:30.376 --> 14:33.004
It's gonna be fine, Amamiya.
It must be rough.

14:33.087 --> 14:35.506
Hey, I just got dumped.

14:35.590 --> 14:37.049
Why don't you comfort me a little?

14:37.133 --> 14:38.426
Well, how many times is it now?

14:38.509 --> 14:40.136
It's starting to be funny.

14:40.219 --> 14:43.222
Though, I'm sure you'll have
a new girlfriend in no time. Darn it, you!

14:43.306 --> 14:46.142
Amamiya, you broke up? Again?

14:46.225 --> 14:47.226
Yup.

14:47.810 --> 14:52.607
She called me out when I was studying
last night. Then she broke up with me.

14:52.690 --> 14:53.858
That's rough.

14:53.941 --> 14:57.236
For some reason, I always get dumped.

14:58.905 --> 15:00.239
Why do you think that is?

15:01.949 --> 15:03.701
WE LET OUR GUARD DOWN,
AND THIS AGAIN - THUMP THUMP

15:03.784 --> 15:05.036
Fujita! Don't let him trick you.

15:05.119 --> 15:06.954
Don't hold eye contact
for longer than three seconds!

15:07.038 --> 15:08.372
Okay.

15:08.456 --> 15:11.250
- I'll hold him down. Now, go!
- Morning… Huh?

15:11.334 --> 15:14.921
Minato, what'd you do this time? Sheesh.

15:15.004 --> 15:18.007
I haven't done a thing. Why do you
always assume I've done something wrong?

15:19.300 --> 15:21.260
<i>Speaking of…</i>

15:27.850 --> 15:30.978
The cafeteria has a lot more options
if you get there early.

15:31.520 --> 15:33.147
- Hey, Yota.
- Yeah?

15:33.731 --> 15:36.651
Weren't you walking home
with Hikawa yesterday?

15:37.234 --> 15:38.653
<i>I'm sure he'd say…</i>

15:38.736 --> 15:41.989
It's not like that!
It's a misunderstanding!

15:42.990 --> 15:44.408
You saw us.

15:44.492 --> 15:45.534
What?

15:46.285 --> 15:49.288
We happened to run into each other,
then decided to walk together.

15:52.625 --> 15:55.836
Of course, yeah.

15:55.920 --> 15:57.296
After all, you're…

16:01.133 --> 16:03.552
NURSE'S OFFICE

16:04.136 --> 16:06.097
Hey, Hikawa. Hello.

16:06.180 --> 16:08.057
Why are you at the nurse's office?
Are you hurt?

16:08.140 --> 16:10.685
No.

16:11.602 --> 16:12.937
What's going on?

16:14.188 --> 16:15.189
Yota.

16:16.148 --> 16:17.441
<i>"Yota"</i>?

16:17.525 --> 16:19.318
Koyun.

16:20.319 --> 16:21.320
<i>"Koyun"</i>?

16:21.404 --> 16:23.823
Are you feeling sick? Are you okay?

16:23.906 --> 16:26.826
I just came to warm up by the heater.

16:26.909 --> 16:29.745
What? Is it even that cold today?

16:29.829 --> 16:31.831
It is, actually.
It's down to nine degrees Celsius.

16:31.914 --> 16:33.124
You're wearing your contacts today?

16:33.207 --> 16:35.835
- <i>She won't even glance at me.</i>
- Yup, totally. Wanna look at them?

16:35.918 --> 16:37.837
- Not really.
- Hey, Hikawa.

16:37.920 --> 16:38.921
SCHOOL NURSE - NORIKO

16:39.005 --> 16:42.258
You're letting the cold air in.
If you're done, then leave.

16:42.341 --> 16:43.342
Shoo, shoo.

16:44.802 --> 16:46.887
We got in trouble.

16:46.971 --> 16:48.764
Noriko's always like that.

16:48.848 --> 16:51.726
Is your next class on the fourth floor?

16:51.809 --> 16:53.728
We're going upstairs too.

16:53.811 --> 16:55.354
No…

16:56.063 --> 16:59.233
I meant to stop by my locker.
It's on the first floor.

16:59.984 --> 17:00.985
Okay.

17:01.068 --> 17:02.153
Well, then…

17:02.236 --> 17:03.237
SCUTTLING AWAY

17:03.320 --> 17:04.780
See you later.

17:06.115 --> 17:07.324
<i>"See you later"</i>?

17:16.167 --> 17:18.919
<i>They happened</i>
<i>to run into each other, right?</i>

17:22.715 --> 17:26.177
Another productive night down!

17:26.844 --> 17:29.513
But there are still concepts
I'm not quite grasping.

17:29.597 --> 17:32.391
Sometimes, I want to talk while studying.

17:32.975 --> 17:35.895
What if we study together in my classroom
after school tomorrow?

17:35.978 --> 17:37.563
I'll help you with what I can.

17:37.646 --> 17:38.939
Are you sure?

17:39.023 --> 17:42.026
I'm counting on you, Yota-sensei!

17:42.109 --> 17:43.652
It's no biggie--

17:44.987 --> 17:46.864
Sensei! I heard a loud thud!

17:46.947 --> 17:48.032
Ouch.

17:48.532 --> 17:50.659
Hey! Does your head hurt?

17:50.743 --> 17:53.454
Well, I'm always bumping
my head into things.

17:55.289 --> 17:57.291
<i>Yota's classroom…</i>

17:58.626 --> 18:00.294
<i>seems noisy.</i>

18:01.462 --> 18:03.047
- It'll be fine.
- What?

18:03.130 --> 18:05.841
The rambunctious ones
take off as soon as the bell rings.

18:05.925 --> 18:07.176
True that.

18:07.259 --> 18:09.470
- <i>He read my mind. I'm embarrassed.</i>
- Koyun's not good with that kinda vibe.

18:09.553 --> 18:11.180
I'M ALL FOR IT THOUGH
CHUCKLE

18:13.766 --> 18:15.935
SEAT FOR ONE

18:19.772 --> 18:22.691
Rock, paper, scissors.

18:24.360 --> 18:25.402
Please, go ahead.

18:26.153 --> 18:27.613
You can take the seat.

18:27.696 --> 18:28.823
PUBLIC FACE

18:28.906 --> 18:31.283
Don't mind us.
We're getting off at the next stop.

18:31.367 --> 18:32.368
What?

18:33.744 --> 18:37.123
<i>Please use the stairs in the center</i>
<i>of the platform to transfer between lines.</i>

18:39.208 --> 18:42.002
- <i>The doors on platform three are closing.</i>
- Quick! Shoot, shoot!

18:45.089 --> 18:46.966
We made it.

18:48.592 --> 18:52.138
Why'd you lie? Just give him the seat.

18:52.221 --> 18:54.765
I got embarrassed.

18:54.849 --> 18:56.767
FOGGY

18:56.851 --> 19:00.646
Shoot, the glass fogs up
when I get close to it.

19:07.111 --> 19:09.029
Now I'm laughing too.

19:13.075 --> 19:15.953
Once the exams are over,
I'm signing up for more shifts at work.

19:16.036 --> 19:18.873
We won't be able to go home together,
but stop by my restaurant sometime, Koyun.

19:18.956 --> 19:20.791
THEY TEND TO TALK A LITTLE MORE
BEFORE THEY SAY GOODBYE

19:20.875 --> 19:24.545
You've never been before.
I'll give you an extra serving of smiles.

19:27.882 --> 19:29.425
<i>Stylish burger!</i>

19:29.508 --> 19:32.303
It's kinda intimidating
to eat there by myself.

19:32.386 --> 19:33.429
I'M A HIGH SCHOOLER

19:33.512 --> 19:35.890
Spending over 1,000 yen on a burger
takes some nerve.

19:35.973 --> 19:38.350
I'll talk to the manager,
he'll hook you up with a discount.

19:38.434 --> 19:40.269
I've got you covered.

19:40.352 --> 19:41.562
MANAGER

19:42.146 --> 19:44.607
If you don't want to come alone,
just bring Yota.

19:45.691 --> 19:47.568
He's got his club activities.

19:51.947 --> 19:53.073
See ya.

19:53.657 --> 19:54.867
See you tomorrow.

20:15.054 --> 20:16.555
The laundry.

20:28.567 --> 20:31.528
<i>Was I smiling?</i>

20:35.658 --> 20:37.493
<i>Today was so much fun.</i>

20:37.576 --> 20:41.121
<i>I can't help but feel giddy</i>
<i>about what tomorrow might bring.</i>

20:43.082 --> 20:44.500
<i>I'm better off on my own.</i>

20:44.583 --> 20:45.751
<i>This is fun.</i>

20:45.834 --> 20:47.253
<i>I'd rather not get involved.</i>

20:47.336 --> 20:48.629
<i>I want to talk to them again.</i>

20:48.712 --> 20:50.256
<i>Why can't they leave me alone?</i>

20:50.339 --> 20:51.632
<i>I'm looking forward to tomorrow.</i>

20:54.093 --> 20:57.638
<i>No part of me is fake, but…</i>

20:58.138 --> 20:59.348
<i>they contradict each other.</i>

21:00.975 --> 21:04.019
<i>What do I really want to do?</i>

21:06.230 --> 21:08.774
<i>I don't understand my own feelings.</i>

21:13.112 --> 21:15.030
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

21:15.114 --> 21:16.615
Sneaking in.

21:17.616 --> 21:20.035
Koyun! Come on in.

21:20.661 --> 21:21.912
Pardon me.

21:24.999 --> 21:27.126
Miki says she's running late.

21:27.876 --> 21:30.004
She pinged me too.

21:30.671 --> 21:33.090
Class 5 has the tendency to drag out HR.

21:34.133 --> 21:36.343
Why don't we make a group chat?

21:37.219 --> 21:38.220
Good idea.

21:39.638 --> 21:40.889
Minato.

21:41.557 --> 21:45.185
Are you two dating?

21:45.811 --> 21:47.438
No. You've got the wrong idea.

21:47.521 --> 21:49.481
Miki will be joining us shortly.

21:49.982 --> 21:52.609
Miki? What's up with your friend group?

21:52.693 --> 21:53.694
RATTLE

21:54.737 --> 21:56.196
Minato, why are you here?

21:56.280 --> 21:58.324
What, am I not supposed to be?

21:58.824 --> 22:00.534
Not at all.

22:01.535 --> 22:03.287
<i>Miki is being herself.</i>

22:03.787 --> 22:05.456
FUNDAMENTALS OF PHYSICS

22:05.539 --> 22:08.125
What's this? Is this a study group?

22:08.208 --> 22:09.209
Bingo.

22:16.050 --> 22:17.051
How fun.

22:17.551 --> 22:19.178
Let me join too.

22:23.223 --> 22:24.224
What?

23:50.269 --> 23:55.274
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
